+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI agents in 2026?
+The strongest repos in this list for broad use are `google/adk-python`, `VoltAgent/voltagent`, `block/goose`, `langchain-ai/open-swe`, `mudler/LocalAI`, `danny-avila/LibreChat`, and `bytedance/UI-TARS-desktop`. Which one is best depends on whether you want a framework, coding agent, browser agent, or self-hosted assistant.
+
+### Which open source AI agents can I self-host?
+`LocalAI`, `LibreChat`, `Khoj`, `DB-GPT`, `DocsGPT`, `Rowboat`, and `Better Chatbot` are all good self-hosted options in this repo. If local inference matters, `LocalAI` is the most direct starting point.
+
+### What is the best open source AI coding agent on GitHub?
+For coding-specific workflows, `Goose`, `Open SWE`, `Plandex`, `Qwen Code`, and `Gemini CLI` are the most relevant entries here. `Goose` and `Open SWE` are especially strong if you want active maintenance plus practical software-engineering workflows.
+
+### Are there open source browser AI agents with public GitHub repos?
+Yes. `UI-TARS Desktop`, `Browser Agent`, `Steel Browser`, `CUA`, and `Browserable` are all public GitHub repositories focused on browser automation, computer use, or desktop interaction.
+
+### Which open source AI agent frameworks are best for developers?
+If you want SDK-style frameworks, start with `google/adk-python`, `google/adk-go`, `VoltAgent/voltagent`, and `OpenAgentsControl`. These are more suitable for building your own product than installing a finished assistant.
+
+### Why are some popular AI tools missing from this awesome list?
+This repo excludes tools that do not have a public `github.com` repository, tools that are primarily proprietary SaaS without an open-source repo, and repos with weak fit for the AI-agent category. The filter is intentionally conservative.
+
+### Do all categories have deep coverage?
+No. This list has solid coverage for frameworks, coding agents, browser agents, self-hosted assistants, and workflow tools. Narrower niches such as finance-only agents, legal-only agents, or database-only agents still have fewer high-signal, broadly maintained repos and are better treated as subcategories in future updates.
